==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term/t|la|lāmentābilis||full of sorrow, mournful; deplorable}}, from {{term/t|la|lāmentor||lament}}, from {{term/t|la|lāmenta||wailing, weeping}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ləˈmɛn.tə.bəl/|/ˈlæm.ən.tə.bəl/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Causing [[sorrow]], [[distress]] or [[regret]]; [[deplorable]], [[pitiful]] or [[distressing]].

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:lamentable]]

